        "## **Prompt Engineering with LangChain for Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG)**\n",
        "\n",
        "This code demonstrates a basic implementation of Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) using LangChain. It showcases how to use prompt engineering techniques to enhance question answering with a large language model (LLM) by retrieving relevant context from a document.\n",
        "\n",
        "**How it Works:**\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Document Preparation:** A longer document (in this case, an article about AI) is provided as the knowledge base. It is split into smaller chunks for easier retrieval.\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Retrieval:** A simple retrieval function simulates a vector search, finding the most relevant chunk based on keyword matching with the user's query.\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Prompt Template:** A PromptTemplate is defined to structure the input for the LLM. It incorporates the retrieved context and the user's question into a clear prompt.\n",
        "\n",
        "4. **LLM Interaction:** An Ollama-backed LLM is initialized through an OpenAI-compatible endpoint and used to generate an answer based on the prompt. The prompt is designed to guide the LLM to use the provided context and answer concisely.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Prompt Engineering Focus:**\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Contextualization:** The prompt template plays a crucial role in providing context to the LLM. It explicitly instructs the LLM to use the retrieved information to answer the question.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Instruction and Formatting:** The prompt includes instructions on how to format the answer (single sentence, bullet point) to ensure consistency and clarity.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Handling Missing Information:** The prompt also provides guidance for cases where no relevant information is found, prompting the LLM to indicate this explicitly."
      ],
      "id": "cd188d9f"
